title: Drop the 64-byte cwd path emulation after the switch
updated: 2026-11-27T15:51:20Z
---

src/loadguard-hook.c builds <root>/proc/<pid>/cwd in a 64-byte buffer (start_run ~2209 and ~2179). With a test root longer than ~45 chars the learned cwd comes out empty; four Watch tests in test_learn and test_parity fail under a long TMPDIR (also on main). Production (empty root) is unaffected. The TS watcher reproduces the limit for parity (k21). Once C is gone (B7, k23), remove the emulation from the TS watcher and its tests.
